# Update the local ROUNDS install

After changing plugin code, build Debug before finishing so the running game folder gets the new DLL.

```powershell
dotnet build RoundsWithFriends/RoundsWithFriends.csproj -c Debug
```

- The post-build script copies `RoundsWithFriends.dll` to `ROUNDS\BepInEx\plugins\olavim-RoundsWithFriends`.
- Use Debug for this. Release also copies the DLL, then packages Thunderstore and GitHub zips. Use Release only when the user asks for a release.
- If the build fails, fix it and build again. Do not leave the game on the previous DLL.
- BepInEx loads the plugin at launch. Tell the user to restart ROUNDS to see the change.
- Skip the build when the change is docs, rules, or other files the game does not load.
